{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>תחד</b> Twice in the Masorah: here and the other <b>לא תחד</b> — in burial. Jacob sought that even after burial they not mention him in the matter of Korah, and this is <b>בקהלם</b>, for it is stated there: <b>ויקהל עליהם קרח</b> (Numbers 16:19). But when tracing their lineage on the dukhan, he did mention them, for it is stated: <b>בן לוי בן ישראל</b> (1 Chronicles 6:1)." "<b>כי באפם הרגו איש</b> in gematria: this is Shechem son of Hamor — <b>שכם בן חמור</b>."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {0 "The second Masorah occurrence 'לא תחד' does not appear in the canonical text as a phrase; likely a Masoretic note referencing a word-level tradition. The verse citation in 1 Chronicles follows the Hebrew verse numbering."}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:18:42.131995964Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}